{"units": [{"id": "endikos-quote12", "translation": "in more just deeds."}, {"id": "endikos-quote13", "translation": "For old age is more just than youth."}, {"id": "endikos-quote14", "translation": "a most just people."}, {"id": "endikos-word1", "translation": "hill"}, {"id": "endikos-word2", "translation": "all-just"}, {"id": "endikos-word3", "translation": "of brave men"}, {"id": "endikos_adv-orth1", "translation": "justly"}, {"id": "endikos_adv-def1", "translation": "justly"}, {"id": "endikos_adv-quote1", "translation": "Except for this, no one could justly blame me."}, {"id": "endikos_adv-quote2", "translation": "It would be rightly and justly named."}, {"id": "endikos_adv-quote3", "translation": "Justice is accomplished justly."}, {"id": "endikos_adv-quote4", "translation": "What of these things do I not justly gather?"}, {"id": "endikos_adv-quote5", "translation": "May the son of Maia justly assist."}, {"id": "endikos_adv-quote6", "translation": "They justly met their fate."}, {"id": "endikos_adv-quote7", "translation": "I deny that you are justly driving Orestes into exile."}, {"id": "endikos_adv-quote8", "translation": "Fearing such a thing, justly revered."}, {"id": "endothen-orth1", "translation": "from within"}, {"id": "endothen-def1", "translation": "from within"}, {"id": "endothen-note1", "translation": "erroneously for ἔντοσθεν [from within], which see."}, {"id": "endothen-quote1", "translation": "But we ourselves are being ravaged from within by our own hands."}, {"id": "endothen-quote2", "translation": "placing bloody ruin from within."}, {"id": "endothen-word1", "translation": "from within"}, {"id": "endon-orth1", "translation": "within"}, {"id": "endon-def1", "translation": "within"}, {"id": "endon-def2", "translation": "at home"}, {"id": "endon-def3", "translation": "Of the mind"}, {"id": "endon-note1", "translation": "Similarly Eur. Heracl. 709 σῶν φρενῶν οὐκ ἔνδον ὤν [not being within your senses], and others mentioned in the Thesaurus vol. 3 p. 1041."}, {"id": "endon-quote1", "translation": "Do not hide it within your heart."}, {"id": "endon-quote2", "translation": "Being within, do not cause harm."}, {"id": "endon-quote3", "translation": "to fight within under cowardice."}, {"id": "endon-quote4", "translation": "Who is within, O child, child, again, in the house?"}, {"id": "endon-quote5", "translation": "Come within, and do not be struck with astonishment in your heart."}, {"id": "endon-word1", "translation": "not being within your senses"}, {"id": "endrosos-orth1", "translation": "dewy"}, {"id": "endrosos-def1", "translation": "dewy"}, {"id": "endrosos-quote1", "translation": "But when I have a night-wandering, dewy bed."}, {"id": "endynasteuo-orth1", "translation": "to rule among"}, {"id": "endynasteuo-def1", "translation": "to rule among"}, {"id": "endynasteuo-quote1", "translation": "I, having ruled among them."}, {"id": "endytos-orth1", "translation": "clothed in"}, {"id": "endytos-def1", "translation": "clothed in"}, {"id": "endytos-quote1", "translation": "in purple-dyed garments."}, {"id": "enezesthai-orth1", "translation": "to sit upon"}, {"id": "enezesthai-def1", "translation": "to sit upon"}, {"id": "enezesthai-note1", "translation": "It is the aorist infinitive of ἐνεζόμην [I sat upon], which alone the old Attic writers use, but later writers also used ἕζομαι [I sit] and its compounds in the present tense: see Thes. vol. 3 p. 1052."}, {"id": "enezesthai-quote1", "translation": "sitting upon this ancient roof."}, {"id": "enezesthai-word1", "translation": "I sat upon"}, {"id": "enezesthai-word2", "translation": "I sit"}, {"id": "eneimi-orth1", "translation": "to be in"}, {"id": "eneimi-def1", "translation": "to be in"}, {"id": "eneimi-def2", "translation": "ἔνι [it is possible] for ἔνεστι [it is possible]"}, {"id": "eneimi-quote1", "translation": "For somehow this disease is inherent in tyranny."}, {"id": "eneimi-quote2", "translation": "In eagerness and daring, what penalty do you see being in it?"}, {"id": "eneimi-quote3", "translation": "Ares is not in it."}, {"id": "eneimi-quote4", "translation": "of the dead, in whom there is no moisture."}, {"id": "eneimi-quote5", "translation": "But you have no strength in you."}, {"id": "eneimi-quote6", "translation": "Nor is it in me to speak with charming tongue in vain."}, {"id": "eneimi-quote7", "translation": "A clear word prevails in this, and there is no strife in it."}, {"id": "eneimi-quote8", "translation": "Ares is not in the land."}, {"id": "eneimi-word1", "translation": "it is possible"}, {"id": "eneimi-word2", "translation": "it is possible"}, {"id": "heneka-orth1", "translation": "for the sake of"}, {"id": "heneka-def1", "translation": "for the sake of"}, {"id": "heneka-note1", "translation": "The other form οὕνεκα [for the sake of] will be discussed in its own place."}, {"id": "heneka-quote1", "translation": "for the sake of Helen."}, {"id": "heneka-quote2", "translation": "For the sake of what harm did you kill my child?"}, {"id": "heneka-word1", "translation": "for the sake of"}, {"id": "enerthe-orth1", "translation": "beneath"}, {"id": "enerthe-def1", "translation": "beneath"}, {"id": "enerthe-def2", "translation": "from below"}, {"id": "enerthe-note1", "translation": "Thus frequently in Euripides and others: see Thes. vol. 3 p. 1068."}, {"id": "enerthe-quote1", "translation": "beneath the earth."}, {"id": "enerthe-quote2", "translation": "beneath the earth."}, {"id": "enerthe-quote3", "translation": "the gods beneath the earth."}, {"id": "enerthe-quote4", "translation": "beneath the earth."}, {"id": "enerthe-quote5", "translation": "to the places beneath and below the earth."}, {"id": "enerthe-quote6", "translation": "to send good things to you and to your child from beneath the earth to the light."}, {"id": "enerthe-quote7", "translation": "send up from below the soul to the light."}, {"id": "eneroi-orth1", "translation": "the dead below"}, {"id": "eneroi-def1", "translation": "the dead below"}, {"id": "eneroi-quote1", "translation": "But he hunts me, wretched, crossing from the dead below."}, {"id": "eneroi-quote2", "translation": "Earth and Hermes, and king of those below."}, {"id": "enechomai-orth1", "translation": "to be held, to be bound"}, {"id": "enechomai-def1", "translation": "to be held, to be bound"}, {"id": "enechomai-note1", "translation": "Thus Porson for ἐνεύξεται [he will boast]."}, {"id": "enechomai-quote1", "translation": "Zeus will be held by unjust words."}, {"id": "enechomai-word1", "translation": "he will boast"}, {"id": "enzeugnymi-orth1", "translation": "to bind fast"}, {"id": "enzeugnymi-def1", "translation": "to bind fast"}, {"id": "enzeugnymi-quote1", "translation": "I am bound by these necessities."}, {"id": "enzeugnymi-quote2", "translation": "You bound me – in misfortunes?"}, {"id": "enelysios-orth1", "translation": "struck by lightning"}, {"id": "enelysios-def1", "translation": "struck by lightning"}]}